  "raw": " and the formation of the Protestant Reformation. The fight for religious liberty became a high priority, with full support of Abraham Lincoln, in order to rebel against the tyranny of government rule.\n\nAmericans have been religiously free since 1623, and the constitution allows them all freedom of religion.\n\nAmericans have been religiously free since 1623, and the constitution allows them all freedom of religion. Christians were always the first people on the side of religious liberty. They ask for and embrace it when they read Scripture. For example, in Matthew Henry’s 45th Psalm, in Fifteenth Sunday after Epiphany, 1671 he said:“Where is the place, O Lord that doth keep the sinners from judgment,Who can hide the ungodly in the dust,Who can hide the unrighteous?” And. in Fifteenth Sunday after Epiphany, 1671 he said:“Where is the wise man that shall undiscover thee?Thou canst",
